Two changes requested.

1. `mm->pinned_vm` is shared with every other pinner in the process (`io_uring`, vfio, RDMA), so a process near its limit through those gets `-ENOMEM` here, and `ctlv_blob_context_fail()` then reports it to userspace as `CTLV_VALIDATION_REASON_BAD_BLOB_DESCRIPTOR`. Report a charge failure with its own reason, or document that it is reported as a bad descriptor.
2. Add a comment above `ctlv_blob_pin_charge()` saying that reading `rlimit()` once and charging `pinned_vm` without `mmap_lock` is deliberate, and why it does not use `__account_locked_vm()`, which does the same under the lock for `locked_vm`.

> +		atomic64_sub(pages_count, &mm->pinned_vm);
> +		return -ENOMEM;
