Drop the three overflow checks and `bytes`. `end <= TASK_SIZE` already bounds everything below: `last >= first`, so the subtraction cannot underflow; `span >> PAGE_SHIFT` is below `ULONG_MAX`, so adding 1 cannot wrap; and `count * sizeof(struct page *)` cannot overflow because `PAGE_SIZE` is much larger than a pointer (`kvmalloc_array()` checks its own multiplication anyway). The function reduces to the `TASK_SIZE` check and `*pages_count = ((last - first) >> PAGE_SHIFT) + 1`.

> +	    check_add_overflow(span >> PAGE_SHIFT, 1UL, &count) ||
> +	    check_mul_overflow(count, sizeof(struct page *), &bytes))
> +		return -EFAULT;
