Summary of the most serious issues in 9/20:
- `ctlv_blob_context_finish()`: the drain loop spins forever if `ctlv_blob_put()` ever fails (it returns `-EINVAL` without unlinking when the task differs), and `ctlv_blob_put()`'s return value is otherwise meaningless.
- `ctx->blob_error` is never set to anything but 0 (or `-EINVAL` in finish itself): a dead field/mechanism. Several !`blob->ctx` / !submitter branches are dead because `resolve()` already guarantees both.
- `ctlv_blob_va_acquire()`: comment says "before charging or allocating", but the `kvmalloc_array()` of a schema-sized page array happens before the `RLIMIT_MEMLOCK` charge; charge first. Also redundant overflow checks in `ctlv_blob_va_range()`, speculative union/type-switch generality while `acquire()` hardcodes VA.
- `ctlv_blob_context_track()` is exported through `blob.h` but only used in `blob.c`; unused includes; a blob resolved from an absent optional attr WARNs (user-triggerable if the family does not guard).
- `ctlv_blob_context_fail()` wipes `ctx->error` (including a message set via `ctlv_op_error()`) and reports `-ENOMEM`/pin failures as `BAD_BLOB_DESCRIPTOR`.
